# Local development only. Public settings are documented in docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
# Ollama model used for photo analysis (read by the app and the AI worker).
# Unset or blank = qwen3-vl:4b-instruct. A malformed value disables analysis.
# Pull it first: ollama pull <this value>. Only the Qwen3-VL 4B (default) and 2B instruct models have been tried, in a few development runs.
# LOCAL RUNS: put shared settings in .env.local (or .env). Next.js reads them for
# the web process and the analysis worker (scripts/analysis-worker.ts) reads the
# same files with Next's own loader (@next/env); a variable already in the shell
# wins. Do not rely on .env.development / .env.production for settings both
# must share. Under Compose (STYLE_PUBLIC_DEPLOYMENT=true) no file is read:
# .env.production feeds both services.
# STYLE_ANALYSIS_MODE (rollback): single = default; multi = earlier multi-item
# behaviour for NEW uploads only (a way back, NOT a validated crowded-photo
# mode). Any other value refuses new uploads.
# Launch information (build 032): where YOUR privacy notice, terms and support
# contact are published. The app links to them at /privacy, /terms and /support
# and redirects there. Required and validated ONLY when STYLE_PUBLIC_DEPLOYMENT=true
# (absolute https URLs on a public host; support may instead be mailto:you@your-domain).
# Leave unset for local use: the three links then show a plain "not available" page.
# Configured links do not make the documents adequate; see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
# STYLE_PRIVACY_URL=
# STYLE_TERMS_URL=
# STYLE_SUPPORT_URL=
VISION_MODEL=qwen3-vl:4b-instruct
STYLE_PUBLIC_DEPLOYMENT=false
APP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434


